Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 18:02:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PS5: the shadow cascades snap to whole texels, so their
 dapple stops crawling; built, untested on console

The game fits the cascaded shadow map to the record camera each frame; a few centimetres of head movement moves that fit by under a texel, and the 2x2 PCF taps then land on different texels, so light through a lattice re-forms every frame. Two native hooks now round the cascade matrices' x/y translation to whole shadow-map texels before the game stores them: ShadowPrePass slot 0 (the three near cascades' render matrices) and DepthShadowProj slot 17 (the per-cascade view-space to shadow-UV matrices). The texel size comes from the Graphics pack's active Shadows preset (High is 2x), frozen at the first frame so a preset saved for the next start cannot change this run's grid. The matrices keep their layout and only x/y move; z is untouched. The pack's asm calls the hooks before its existing capture. One boot log line: Shadow cascades: 1-texel snap on, Shadows "High (200%)" (2.00x).
